{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T082511Z_dev-03_staged_aef8", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "In Kim, Lee, Park and Shin (arXiv:1601.05089), the best fit for ψψ̄ → h2h2 (about 100% of annihilation) used m_ψ = 69.2 GeV and m_h2 = 35.7 GeV. They gave ⟨σv⟩ = 2.26×10^-26 cm^3 s^-1, with Ωh² = 0.121. The J-factor was rescaled by 𝒥 = 2.2 times the canonical value, i.e. J̄ = 2.2 × J̄_canonical, where J̄_canonical ≃ 2×10^23 GeV²/cm⁵. This gave χ² = 23.19 (p-value 0.39).", "found": true, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "1601.05089v3", "section_id": "3"}]}, "turns": 5, "seconds": 13.822, "tool_calls": 6, "tool_result_chars": 30237, "input_tokens": 12, "output_tokens": 948, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 14895, "cache_read_input_tokens": 20728, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:25:25+00:00"}
